<title>USA: CME feeder cattle sharply higher-limit up.</title>
<headline>CME feeder cattle sharply higher-limit up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME feeder cattle futures were sharply higher to up the 1.50-cent-a-lb limit at mid-morning, boosted by commercial as well as commission house buying.</p>
<p>Floor sources said Refco, Cargill and Rand Financials were all featured buyers.</p>
<p>At 1020 CDT August was up 0.750 cent at 81.150 cents a lb with January rising the 1.50 cent limit to 83.250 cent.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
